    "body": "## Question\n\nBoth Codex (OpenAI) and Claude Code (Anthropic) now implement **background / silent computer-use on macOS** \u2014 the agent can drive the UI (clicks, typing, screenshots) without stealing foreground window focus, so the user can keep working in another app while the agent operates.\n\n**Does Orca's macOS computer-use (`orca computer \u2026`) also operate silently / in the background, or does it require (and grab) foreground focus?**\n\nIf it does grab focus today: is silent background computer-use on macOS on the roadmap, and is the focus-stealing considered expected behavior or a bug to fix?\n\n## What I observed\n\nOn my machine, during computer-use operations Orca appears to **grab / steal the foreground window** (the target app, or sometimes Orca itself, jumps to the front), which is exactly the behavior Codex and Claude Code have moved away from. I want to confirm whether this is intended or a known limitation before reporting it as a pure bug.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Orca: 1.4.194 (build 1.4.194)\n- OS: macOS 15.7.7 (Build 24G720), Apple Silicon (arm64)\n- Computer-use provider: default (whatever `orca computer capabilities` advertises on this install)\n\n## Related issues\n\n- #16674 \u2014 Windows browser automation stealing foreground focus (no flag to disable). Same class of problem, but Windows + browser only.\n- #15954 \u2014 Feature request for a `cua-driver` computer-use provider with background input. Suggests background input is not yet generally available.\n- #12592 \u2014 macOS `orca computer click --x/--y` no-op (closed). Hints the macOS computer-use path has had focus/activation gaps before.\n\n## Ask\n\n1. Is silent / background computer-use on macOS supported today (or planned)?\n2. If not, is the foreground-focus grabbing I'm seeing expected, and is there a setting/flag to suppress it?\n\nHappy to turn this into a proper `[Bug]:` report with repro steps if the focus-stealing is unintended.",
